---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "@utils/site";
const updated = "2026-05-13";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Pocketey handles cookies, analytics, and advertising data. We list every third-party vendor we use and what kind of cookie each one sets."
  pageType="static"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-amber-400 text-stroke-ink">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-60">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      This page explains what data {SITE.name} collects when you visit the
      site or play one of the games, what we use it for, and what choices you
      have. Plain English first, formal language second.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Who we are</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      {SITE.name} is a small, independently operated game site reachable at
      {SITE.url}. It is run by a solo developer rather than a company, and is
      hosted on Cloudflare Pages.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">What we collect</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      The site itself uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is a cookieless
      analytics product. It records aggregate page views, country-level
      geography, the referring site, and basic information about your browser
      such as the user agent string. It does not assign you a persistent
      identifier, does not build a behavior profile, and does not share your
      data with third-party advertising networks. We do not run any other
      first-party analytics tool by default.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      Each individual game stores a small amount of progress data inside your
      browser using <code>localStorage</code>. This typically includes high
      scores, the level you reached, your sound preference, and similar
      gameplay state. None of this leaves your device. You can clear it at any
      time by clearing site data for {SITE.url} in your browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      We group cookies and similar storage (localStorage, web beacons, pixel
      tags, device identifiers) into three categories so it is clear what each
      one does and who sets it.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/20">
            <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-extrabold">Category</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-extrabold">Purpose</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-extrabold">Set by</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Strictly necessary</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Keep the site working: deliver pages, remember your sound /
              language preference, store local game progress.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">{SITE.name} (localStorage), Cloudflare</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Statistics</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Aggregate, anonymous traffic measurement only. No persistent
              identifier, no cross-site tracking, no profile.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">Cloudflare Web Analytics (cookieless)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Advertising</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Serve ads, measure performance, and (with your consent in
              regions where required) personalize ads based on your interests.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">Google AdSense, Google Funding Choices</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Advertising</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      Some pages display advertising provided by Google AdSense. As an
      independent ad network, Google and its partners may set their own
      cookies, web beacons or device identifiers in order to serve, measure
      and report on ads, and — depending on the consent you give — to
      personalize ads on other sites you visit. Pocketey itself never receives
      personal data from these networks; we only see aggregate revenue and
      performance reports.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      For visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK, and Switzerland, we
      use Google's <strong>Funding Choices</strong> consent management
      platform to ask whether you accept personalized ads before any
      advertising cookies are set. You can change that choice at any time by
      clearing site cookies and reloading the page, or via the link in the
      consent dialog.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      You can review and adjust the choices Google makes about your ads at
      <a class="underline" href="https://adssettings.google.com/">adssettings.google.com</a>.
      You can opt out of personalized advertising from many third-party
      networks at the
      <a class="underline" href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/">Network Advertising Initiative</a>
      and the
      <a class="underline" href="https://optout.aboutads.info/">Digital Advertising Alliance</a>.
      California residents have additional rights, including the right to opt
      out of the sale or sharing of personal information, which you can
      exercise via the links above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Third-party vendors</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      The following independent companies process limited data when you use
      the site. Each link goes to that vendor's own privacy policy, which
      governs how they handle the data they receive.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/20">
            <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-extrabold">Vendor</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-extrabold">What it does</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-extrabold">Policy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Cloudflare Pages</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">Static site hosting and global CDN delivery.</td>
            <td class="py-2">
              <a class="underline" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">cloudflare.com</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Cloudflare Web Analytics</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Cookieless, aggregate traffic measurement. No persistent
              identifier.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">
              <a class="underline" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">cloudflare.com</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Google AdSense</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Display advertising. May set cookies for ad delivery,
              measurement and (with consent) personalization.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">
              <a class="underline" href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">policies.google.com</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Google Funding Choices</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Consent management platform shown to EEA / UK / Swiss visitors
              before advertising cookies are set.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">
              <a class="underline" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1a0a30]/10 align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Google Fonts</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Serves the Fredoka web font. Receives the standard request
              headers a font asset request entails (IP, user agent, referer).
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">
              <a class="underline" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="align-top">
            <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold">Resend</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-3">
              Used only when you submit player feedback through the in-game
              widget; relays the message to the operator's email.
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">
              <a class="underline" href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">resend.com</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Player feedback widget</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      Each game has an optional 👍 / 👎 / 🐛 feedback widget. If you choose to
      submit feedback, the rating and any free-text comment you write are sent
      through Cloudflare Functions to the site operator's email via Resend.
      We do not collect your name, email, or any other identifier unless you
      include it in the comment yourself.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Children</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      The site is not directed at children under 13 (or the equivalent
      minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal
      information to us, please reach out via the contact page and we will
      delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">International transfers</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      Because the site is delivered through Cloudflare's global content
      delivery network, requests are routed to the data center closest to the
      visitor. Cloudflare and Google operate infrastructure across many
      countries; their respective privacy policies (linked above) cover how
      they handle traffic data in transit and at rest.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Your choices</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      You can disable JavaScript or use an ad blocker to opt out of
      advertising on the site. You can withdraw consent for personalized ads
      at any time by clearing cookies for {SITE.url} and reloading; the
      Funding Choices dialog will appear again. You can clear local game
      progress at any time via your browser. You can request information
      about data we hold by emailing the address on the contact page; because
      we operate at a small scale, we typically have very little data
      attached to any one visitor.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      When we change anything material on this page, we will update the date
      at the top of the document and, where the change affects how data is
      collected, post a short notice on the home page. Continued use of the
      site after such a change means you accept the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      Questions about this policy can be sent through the
      <a class="underline" href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We try to
      respond within a few business days.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
